  "name": "ANTI PHOSPHOLPID ANTIBODY - IgA (APL - IgA)",
  "code": "APLIGA",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"185\" data-end=\"333\">\n<p data-start=\"187\" data-end=\"333\">Anti-phospholipid antibodies (aPL) are autoantibodies directed against phospholipids or phospholipid-binding proteins (e.g., &beta;2-glycoprotein I).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"334\" data-end=\"399\">\n<p data-start=\"336\" data-end=\"399\">The main antibody classes measured are <strong data-start=\"375\" data-end=\"396\">IgG, IgM, and IgA</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"580\">\n<p data-start=\"402\" data-end=\"483\">They are associated with <strong data-start=\"427\" data-end=\"463\">Anti-Phospholipid Syndrome (APS)</strong>, which can cause:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"486\" data-end=\"580\">\n<li data-start=\"486\" data-end=\"526\">\n<p data-start=\"488\" data-end=\"526\">Recurrent arterial/venous thrombosis</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"529\" data-end=\"557\">\n<p data-start=\"531\" data-end=\"557\">Recurrent pregnancy loss</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"560\" data-end=\"580\">\n<p data-start=\"562\" data-end=\"580\">Thrombocytopenia</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Meaning</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative (Not detected)</strong></td>\n<td>No significant IgA anti-phospholipid antibodies. Usually rules out APS related to IgA isotype.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low/Borderline Positive</strong></td>\n<td>May be nonspecific; sometimes seen in infections, autoimmune conditions, or transiently after illness. Requires repeat testing in 12 weeks if clinically relevant.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive (Elevated levels)</strong></td>\n<td>Suggests presence of IgA aPL. Supports diagnosis of <strong>APS</strong> if clinical features (thrombosis, pregnancy morbidity) are present. Must be confirmed with persistent positivity on repeat testing (&ge;12 weeks apart).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
